</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span><span id="S3.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The AnyGoal architecture.</span> A single forward path runs at
every agent: the multi-modal goal token <math id="S3.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and an RGB-D observation are
processed by a <em id="S3.F1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">swappable</em> open-vocabulary perception stack (SAM3,
GroundedSAM, or YOLO-World, plus a spatial VLM). Detections are
back-projected by the GoalProjector into the shared 2D Gaussian Bayesian
Value Map (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.2 Gaussian Bayesian Value Map ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)). The decentralized coordination
layer scores frontiers via a VLM-as-judge softmax convex-blended with a
Bayesian UCB term (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.3 VLM-as-judge frontier ranking and convex-blended UCB ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)) and allocates them across agents
under a multiplicative separation penalty (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.4 Decentralized swarm coordination ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)). The
mapping and coordination blocks (dashed box) are the only shared substrate;
no centralized controller and no explicit inter-agent message channel are
required.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>System architecture</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">AnyGoal is structured as four <em id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">swappable</em> layers
(Fig. <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). At each decision step, every agent <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> runs the same
local pipeline:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.4em;">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Perception.</span> An open-vocabulary segmentation backbone
(SAM3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> by default; GroundedSAM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>
and YOLO-World <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite> as ablations) emits
goal-conditioned masks; a spatial VLM (SpaceOM-3B) provides relevance
scores; and for image-goal subtasks an image matcher
(CLIP ViT-B/32 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> by default;
DINOv2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> as ablation) supplies similarity to the
reference image.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mapping.</span> Detections are back-projected through depth into a
shared BEV occupancy grid at <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05\,\mathrm{m}/\text{cell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mtext>cell</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05\,\mathrm{m}/\text{cell}</annotation></semantics></math> by a
<em id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GoalProjector</em> that rejects spatially inconsistent VLM hits; the
Bayesian Value Map (§<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Gaussian Bayesian Value Map ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>) maintains goal-relevance
belief on the same grid.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reasoning.</span> A four-stage prompt chain renders the egocentric
view plus candidate frontiers as A/B/C/D markers; the VLM emits (a) a
scene caption, (b) a room-type prior, (c) an “is-worth-pursuing” Yes/No
gate, and (d) a softmax over the frontier markers
(§<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 VLM-as-judge frontier ranking and convex-blended UCB ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Planning.</span> Frontier extraction (connected-component
boundaries on the shared BEV), convex-blended scoring, and a
Fast-Marching-Method (FMM) planner <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> produce a
discrete action in the Habitat action space <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The same code path runs at every agent: only the shared BEV and BVM act as
implicit communication.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Gaussian Bayesian Value Map</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\{(x,y)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\{(x,y)\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the BEV grid. We attach to each cell
<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> a scalar belief over the probability that <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> contains, or is in the
immediate spatial neighborhood of, the current goal:
<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Bel}(p)=\mathcal{N}(\mu(p),\sigma^{2}(p))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Bel</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Bel}(p)=\mathcal{N}(\mu(p),\sigma^{2}(p))</annotation></semantics></math>. The prior is uniform,
<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}\!=\!0.5,\ \sigma_{0}^{2}\!=\!0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}\!=\!0.5,\ \sigma_{0}^{2}\!=\!0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. At each step every visible cell
receives a new observation
<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{\text{obs}},\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>obs</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>obs</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{\text{obs}},\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\text{obs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>obs</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\text{obs}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
the VLM relevance score projected through the depth-cone visibility mask
and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2}=1-\mathrm{cone\_conf}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>obs</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cone</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>conf</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2}=1-\mathrm{cone\_conf}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> encodes how
well-supported the projection is by depth. Posterior fusion is the
standard precision-weighted product of Gaussians:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\text{new}}\;=\;\frac{\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2}\,\mu_{\text{prior}}+\sigma_{\text{prior}}^{2}\,\mu_{\text{obs}}}{\sigma_{\text{prior}}^{2}+\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2}},\qquad\sigma_{\text{new}}^{2}\;=\;\frac{\sigma_{\text{prior}}^{2}\,\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2}}{\sigma_{\text{prior}}^{2}+\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>obs</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>prior</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>prior</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>obs</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>prior</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>obs</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>new</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>prior</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>obs</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>prior</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>obs</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\text{new}}\;=\;\frac{\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2}\,\mu_{\text{prior}}+\sigma_{\text{prior}}^{2}\,\mu_{\text{obs}}}{\sigma_{\text{prior}}^{2}+\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2}},\qquad\sigma_{\text{new}}^{2}\;=\;\frac{\sigma_{\text{prior}}^{2}\,\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2}}{\sigma_{\text{prior}}^{2}+\sigma_{\text{obs}}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.2 Gaussian Bayesian Value Map ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) ensures that high-cone-confidence pixels
(sharp depth) dominate the prior while repeated low-confidence observations
decay rather than reinforce an erroneous belief. The BVM is <em id="S3.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">never
reset between subtasks</em>: when the goal token changes, only the VLM scoring
head changes while accumulated geometric and semantic evidence persists,
yielding lifelong evidence carry-over across the <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> subtasks per
episode. Across <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> agents, the swarm posterior is the precision-weighted
fusion of the agent-local beliefs, applied element-wise on the shared
BEV/BVM tensor.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>VLM-as-judge frontier ranking and convex-blended UCB</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of frontier cells at step <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> extracted from
the connected-component boundary of the explored area on the shared BEV.
We rank <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by fusing <em id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">spatial geometry</em> with <em id="S3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">VLM
common sense</em>. Up to four salient frontiers are rendered onto the
egocentric image as labeled markers <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A,B,C,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A,B,C,D\}</annotation></semantics></math> and submitted, alongside
the current goal token, to a VLM-as-judge prompt; the VLM returns a
softmax <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{VLM}}(f)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{VLM}}(f)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> over the markers. In parallel, each
frontier inherits the BVM statistics of its anchor cell and yields a
Bayesian Upper-Confidence-Bound score</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{UCB}(f)\;=\;\mu(f)\;+\;\beta\,\sqrt{\sigma^{2}(f)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>UCB</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{UCB}(f)\;=\;\mu(f)\;+\;\beta\,\sqrt{\sigma^{2}(f)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\!&gt;\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\!&gt;\!0</annotation></semantics></math> controls the exploration weight; the resulting score
inflates the value of cells that are believed relevant on average
<em id="S3.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">or</em> have not been sufficiently observed. The two signals are
combined through a convex blend</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(f)\;=\;(1-w)\,p_{\text{VLM}}(f)\;+\;w\,\widetilde{\mathrm{UCB}}(f),\qquad w=0.50," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>UCB</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(f)\;=\;(1-w)\,p_{\text{VLM}}(f)\;+\;w\,\widetilde{\mathrm{UCB}}(f),\qquad w=0.50,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathrm{UCB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>UCB</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathrm{UCB}}</annotation></semantics></math> is min-max normalized over <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Eq. (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.3 VLM-as-judge frontier ranking and convex-blended UCB ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) treats the VLM as a high-noise oracle on
<em id="S3.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">plausibility</em> and the BVM as a low-noise oracle on <em id="S3.SS3.p1.3.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">coverage</em>;
neither fully overrules the other. An explicit <em id="S3.SS3.p1.3.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">is-worth</em> gate, a
Yes/No VLM prompt with threshold
<math id="S3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Perception\_PR}(f)\!\geq\!0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Perception</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>PR</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Perception\_PR}(f)\!\geq\!0.50</annotation></semantics></math>, vetoes candidates the VLM
considers structurally implausible (e.g. a refrigerator frontier inside
an already-explored bathroom).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Decentralized swarm coordination</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">AnyGoal is decentralized in the <em id="S3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">planning</em> sense: no centralized
controller selects frontiers or actions, no inter-agent reward is shared,
and there is no explicit message channel beyond synchronization of the
shared BEV/BVM, which is a fused observation rather than a command
substrate. Allocation proceeds
by <em id="S3.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sequential greedy bidding</em>: at each re-evaluation step, agents
are indexed in a fixed deterministic order; agent <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> picks</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}^{\star}\;=\;\arg\max_{f\in\mathcal{F}_{t}}\;s(f)\cdot\prod_{j&lt;i}\,\phi\!\big(d(f,f_{j}^{\star})\big),\qquad\phi(d)=\begin{cases}0.60&amp;d&lt;100\,\text{px}\\
1.00&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.426em;" width="0.426em"><mi>ϕ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.60</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>px</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1.00</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}^{\star}\;=\;\arg\max_{f\in\mathcal{F}_{t}}\;s(f)\cdot\prod_{j&lt;i}\,\phi\!\big(d(f,f_{j}^{\star})\big),\qquad\phi(d)=\begin{cases}0.60&amp;d&lt;100\,\text{px}\\
1.00&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is BEV pixel distance. The multiplicative penalty
discourages two agents from converging on the same frontier without ever
instantiating a joint optimization problem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Frontier re-evaluation is gated to every <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=25</annotation></semantics></math> steps: between
re-evaluations each agent simply follows its FMM plan towards
<math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. Together with a <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5\!\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\!\times</annotation></semantics></math> commitment hysteresis, an
agent switches from <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{prev}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>prev</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{prev}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{new}}</annotation></semantics></math> only when
<math id="S3.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(f_{\text{new}})\geq 1.5\,s(f_{\text{prev}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>prev</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(f_{\text{new}})\geq 1.5\,s(f_{\text{prev}})</annotation></semantics></math>, this prevents the
high-frequency frontier oscillations that we observed in early prototypes
when the VLM softmax fluctuated between near-tied candidates. The shared
map itself is the only coordination channel: BEV occupancy is element-wise
max-fused across agents, and the BVM is fused by the same Gaussian
product as Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.2 Gaussian Bayesian Value Map ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experimental Setup</h2>

<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Benchmark and simulator.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate on the full <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GOAT-Bench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>
<em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">val_unseen</em> split: <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="360" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>360</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">360</annotation></semantics></math> photorealistic HM3D
episodes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> heterogeneous subtasks per
episode (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2{,}669" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2,669</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2{,}669</annotation></semantics></math> subtasks in the primary evaluation), <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="36" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>36</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">36</annotation></semantics></math> goal
categories, and three goal modalities (object name, RGB image, free-form
language description) interleaved within a single episode. The maximum
subtask budget is <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">500</annotation></semantics></math> steps; the success radius is <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\,\mathrm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\,\mathrm{m}</annotation></semantics></math> from
any instance of the goal. We use Habitat-Lab and
Habitat-Sim <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> (tag
<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">challenge-2022</span>) with the Stretch embodiment (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.41</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.41</annotation></semantics></math> m
height, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.17</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.17</annotation></semantics></math> m radius, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.31" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.31</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.31</annotation></semantics></math> m camera height) and
<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">allow_sliding=False</span>. Each agent has a forward-facing
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="360\!\times\!640" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>640</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">360\!\times\!640</annotation></semantics></math> RGB-D sensor at <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="42^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>42</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">42^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> HFOV plus GPS/compass;
the action space is the discrete <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textsc{move\_forward},\textsc{turn\_left},\textsc{turn\_right},\textsc{stop}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">move_forward</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">turn_left</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">turn_right</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textsc{move\_forward},\textsc{turn\_left},\textsc{turn\_right},\textsc{stop}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Metrics.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report standard <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GOAT-Bench</span> metrics: <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Subtask SR</span>
(<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</span> within <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\,\mathrm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\,\mathrm{m}</annotation></semantics></math> of any goal instance in <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq\!500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq\!500</annotation></semantics></math>
steps), <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SPL</span> (geodesic-weighted), <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SoftSPL</span>, <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DTG</span>
(mean distance-to-goal at <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</span>), and episode-perfect
<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Episode SR</span>. We additionally split failures into <em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">false stops</em>
(<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{euc}}\!&gt;\!1\,\mathrm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>euc</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{euc}}\!&gt;\!1\,\mathrm{m}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">budget exhaustion</em> (no
<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</span> within <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">500</annotation></semantics></math> steps); the latter is critical for the
perception ablation of Section <a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Perception bottleneck ablation (the 4-way test) ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Configurations.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless stated otherwise, AnyGoal runs with <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!2</annotation></semantics></math> homogeneous ground
agents, SAM3 perception, SpaceOM-3B VLM, and CLIP ViT-B/32 as image
matcher. Architectural hyperparameters are fixed at the values introduced
in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>: <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\!=\!0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\!=\!0.50</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\!=\!25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\!=\!25</annotation></semantics></math> steps,
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5\!\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\!\times</annotation></semantics></math> commitment hysteresis, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100\,\mathrm{px}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>px</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100\,\mathrm{px}</annotation></semantics></math> separation
threshold with <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.6</annotation></semantics></math> penalty, and “is-worth” threshold <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.50</annotation></semantics></math>; the UCB
coefficient <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and remaining implementation constants follow the
released codebase.<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            Anonymous code release:
<a href="https://anonymous.4open.science/r/anygoal-B855/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://anonymous.4open.science/r/anygoal-B855/</a>.</span></span></span> In ablations,
GroundedSAM uses tuned thresholds (box <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.55</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.55</annotation></semantics></math>, text <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.40</annotation></semantics></math>) and
YOLO-World uses confidence threshold <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.30</annotation></semantics></math> (coarse-grid search,
appendix).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hyperparameter rationale and single-run protocol.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The map resolution (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05\,\mathrm{m}/\text{cell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mtext>cell</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05\,\mathrm{m}/\text{cell}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="480\!\times\!480" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>480</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">480\!\times\!480</annotation></semantics></math>
grid) lets the <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\,\mathrm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\,\mathrm{m}</annotation></semantics></math> success radius span <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> cells, matching
the fine end of the <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\,\mathrm{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\,\mathrm{cm}</annotation></semantics></math> range in VLFM and
Modular GOAT; the convex weight <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\!=\!0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\!=\!0.50</annotation></semantics></math>, hysteresis
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5\!\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\!\times</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100\,\mathrm{px}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>px</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100\,\mathrm{px}</annotation></semantics></math> separation penalty are zero-shot
defaults whose provenance is tabulated in
Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Hyperparameter manifest ‣ Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. A full <em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">val_unseen</em> run takes
2.2–6.0 days on a single RTX 4090, so every ablation cell is a single
full-split rollout under fixed VLM temperatures and deterministic
simulator seeds; a two-seed evaluation of the headline configuration
agrees to within <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math> pp on Subtask SR (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="52.4\,\%\pm 0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>52.4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">52.4\,\%\pm 0.2</annotation></semantics></math> pp,
Appendix <a href="#A4.SS5" title="D.5 Headline-run reproducibility ‣ Appendix D Extended Results ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Real-world transfer.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">AnyGoal ports to a heterogeneous Unitree Go1 + wheeled-platform swarm
by replacing the SAM3+SpaceOM cloud stack with an onboard
YOLO-World+MobileSAM+CLIP edge stack on Jetson AGX Orin (full
hardware, mapping, and ROS2 configuration in Appendix <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Real-World Heterogeneous Deployment ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Results and Evaluation</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>State-of-the-art performance in the strict physical regime</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Across the 360-episode headline run, successful subtasks resolve in
<span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">83 steps</span> on average (17 % of the 500-step budget), while
failing subtasks consume <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">161 steps</span> on average; the median
subtask length is 52 steps. This gap confirms that failures are
dominated by premature <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</span> calls rather than incomplete
exploration, consistent with the <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80.2\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>80.2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80.2\,\%</annotation></semantics></math> false-stop rate in
§<a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Perception bottleneck ablation (the 4-way test) ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Within the strict physical regime that mirrors deployable robot
hardware</span> (discrete <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25\,\mathrm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25\,\mathrm{m}</annotation></semantics></math> forward steps, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="42^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>42</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">42^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> HFOV
matching the HelloRobot Stretch, no continuous teleportation), AnyGoal
with <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!2</annotation></semantics></math> achieves <span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">52.4 %</span> Subtask SR at <span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12.7 %</span>
SPL on <span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GOAT-Bench</span> <em id="S5.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">val_unseen</em> (Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.1 State-of-the-art performance in the strict physical regime ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, top
block), outperforming the official Modular GOAT baseline by
<span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">+27.5 percentage points</span> on Subtask SR, a <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{+110\,\%}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏𝟏𝟎</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{+110\,\%}</annotation></semantics></math>
relative gain, while also exceeding SenseAct-NN Skill Chain by
<math id="S5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+22.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>22.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+22.9</annotation></semantics></math> pp and the strongest prior zero-shot single-agent system,
TANGO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, by <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+20.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>20.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+20.3</annotation></semantics></math> pp. Even the single-agent
configuration alone reaches <span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">41.9 %</span> SR, exceeding every
strict-regime prior system by <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+9.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>9.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+9.8</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+17.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>17.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+17.0</annotation></semantics></math> pp: the architectural
gain therefore originates from the Gaussian BVM, the convex-blended UCB
ranking, and the “is-worth” verification gate rather than from raw
agent count.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The lower block of Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.1 State-of-the-art performance in the strict physical regime ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> lists 3D-Mem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>
under a <em id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">relaxed continuous regime</em> in which the simulator’s action
space and sensor footprint are altered; we discuss why those metrics are
not on the same scale as the strict-regime numbers in §<a href="#S6" title="6 Discussion ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span><span id="S5.T1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Zero-shot performance on <span id="S5.T1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GOAT-Bench</span>
<em id="S5.T1.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">val_unseen</em></span> (360 episodes, full 2,669-subtask split),
partitioned by simulation regime. AnyGoal sets a new state-of-the-art
in the <em id="S5.T1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">strict physical regime</em>, beating Modular GOAT by
<math id="S5.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{+27.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">27.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{+27.5}</annotation></semantics></math> pp on Subtask SR. <em id="S5.T1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Relaxed continuous regime</em>
methods alter the simulator’s action and sensor model; their numbers
are not directly comparable (§<a href="#S6" title="6 Discussion ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</figcaption>
