<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Multi-agent scaling: <math id="S5.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!1\!\rightarrow\!2\!\rightarrow\!3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!1\!\rightarrow\!2\!\rightarrow\!3</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<figure id="S5.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.13878v1/fig_scaling.svg" id="S5.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/168;" width="286" height="168"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span><span id="S5.F2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Swarm scaling on <span id="S5.F2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GOAT-Bench</span> <em id="S5.F2.3.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">val_unseen</em>.</span>
With the AnyGoal architecture held fixed (SAM3 perception, SpaceOM VLM,
CLIP image matcher, BVM, convex-blended UCB, FMM planner) and only the
number of agents varied, Subtask SR rises by <math id="S5.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+10.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>10.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+10.5</annotation></semantics></math> pp
(<math id="S5.F2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!1\!\rightarrow\!2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!1\!\rightarrow\!2</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="S5.F2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+3.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+3.2</annotation></semantics></math> pp (<math id="S5.F2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!2\!\rightarrow\!3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!2\!\rightarrow\!3</annotation></semantics></math>);
SPL declines modestly (<math id="S5.F2.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="14.4\!\to\!12.7\!\to\!11.8\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.484em;" width="0.484em"><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>11.8</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14.4\!\to\!12.7\!\to\!11.8\,\%</annotation></semantics></math>), reflecting
extra total trajectory length traded for the SR gain. The <math id="S5.F2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!3</annotation></semantics></math>
gain is concentrated in description and image-goal modalities, while
object SR is near-saturated at <math id="S5.F2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!2</annotation></semantics></math> (see §<a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Multi-agent scaling: 𝑁=→→3 ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Holding the AnyGoal architecture fixed and varying only the number of
agents traces a monotonic scaling curve
(Fig. <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 5.2 Multi-agent scaling: 𝑁=→→3 ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>): Subtask SR rises <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="41.9\!\to\!52.4\!\to\!55.6\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.484em;" width="0.484em"><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>55.6</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">41.9\!\to\!52.4\!\to\!55.6\,\%</annotation></semantics></math>
for <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!1,2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!1,2,3</annotation></semantics></math>. The first step (<math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+10.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>10.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+10.5</annotation></semantics></math> pp) is the largest and the
second (<math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+3.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+3.2</annotation></semantics></math> pp) is smaller, consistent with diminishing returns as
frontier supply saturates. The <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!3</annotation></semantics></math> gain is concentrated in
description and image-goal modalities (Appendix <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Per-modality × per-𝑁 subtask success rate ‣ Appendix D Extended Results ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>);
object-name navigation is already near-saturated at <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!2</annotation></semantics></math> because
open-vocabulary detectors fire reliably on named objects within two
agents’ combined field of view.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The architectural lesson is independent of agent count: even at
<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!1</annotation></semantics></math>, AnyGoal exceeds Modular GOAT, SenseAct-NN Skill Chain, and
TANGO by <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+9.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>9.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+9.8</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+17.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>17.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+17.0</annotation></semantics></math> pp (Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.1 State-of-the-art performance in the strict physical regime ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), so the Gaussian
BVM, UCB blend, and “is-worth” gate drive most of the gap to prior
art before any multi-agent contribution. The additional <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+10.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>10.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+10.5</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+3.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+3.2</annotation></semantics></math> pp at <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!2,3</annotation></semantics></math> are consistent with later agents mitigating
the single-viewpoint failure modes that bound 3D-Mem-style snapshots:
a hallucination from agent <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with low cone-confidence is rapidly
down-weighted by a high-confidence contradiction from agent <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> via
Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.2 Gaussian Bayesian Value Map ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), without either modeling the other’s
belief explicitly, and <em id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">without any centralized controller</em>, since
only the shared BEV/BVM and the separation penalty
(Eq. (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.4 Decentralized swarm coordination ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)) couple the agents <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Perception bottleneck ablation (the 4-way test)</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We run the full <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GOAT-Bench</span> <em id="S5.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">val_unseen</em> pipeline four times
under identical hyperparameters, varying only the perception backbone
(Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 5.3 Perception bottleneck ablation (the 4-way test) ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). SAM3<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>CLIP achieves the highest
Subtask SR (<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="52.4\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>52.4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">52.4\,\%</annotation></semantics></math>); swapping CLIP for DINOv2 trades <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.7</annotation></semantics></math> pp of SR
for marginal SPL gain, GroundedSAM costs <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.6</annotation></semantics></math> pp, and
YOLO-World<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>MobileSAM costs <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10.4</annotation></semantics></math> pp. Two-proportion <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>-tests
(Appendix <a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Two-proportion 𝑧-tests for Table ‣ Appendix D Extended Results ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>) confirm a recall-tier transition: SAM3-class
detectors are significantly stronger than the GroundedSAM/YOLO-World
tier (<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\!&lt;\!10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">&lt;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\!&lt;\!10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>), while within-tier gaps are not significant at
<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.05</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:189.8pt;">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S5.T2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:189.8pt;height:20.3pt;vertical-align:-9.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-192.8pt,20.7pt) scale(0.32985394333887,0.32985394333887) ;">
