</table>
</span></div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S5.T2.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><sup id="S5.T2.2.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">♭</span></sup>359/360 ep completed; reported value is <math id="S5.F3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.420\pm 0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.420</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.420\pm 0.001</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Table 2: </span><span id="S5.T2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Perception backbone ablation on <span id="S5.T2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GOAT-Bench</span> <em id="S5.T2.6.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">val_unseen</em>.</span> All other components… are held fixed. The <em id="S5.T2.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">failure-mode shift</em> is the central scientific finding.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F3.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:144.9pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.13878v1/fig_ablation.svg" id="S5.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:200/115;" width="200" height="115"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span><span id="S5.F3.fig2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Failure-mode shift.</span> As detector recall increases (right-to-left), budget exhaustion collapses, and false stops dominate.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The deeper finding (right-hand columns of Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 5.3 Perception bottleneck ablation (the 4-way test) ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>;
Fig. <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5.3 Perception bottleneck ablation (the 4-way test) ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>): as detector recall increases, the failure
composition flips, from <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="42.3\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>42.3</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">42.3\,\%</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">budget exhaustion</em> under the
cautious YOLO-World<math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>MobileSAM (the detector never returns a valid
mask in <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">500</annotation></semantics></math> steps) to <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80.2\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>80.2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80.2\,\%</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="S5.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">false stops</em> under SAM3<math id="S5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>CLIP
(the agent rarely fails to <em id="S5.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">find</em> a candidate but fails to
<em id="S5.SS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">verify</em> it). This is, to our knowledge, the first controlled,
like-for-like demonstration that the bottleneck of zero-shot VLM
navigation has shifted: for closed-set systems <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>
the limiter is detector recall; for SAM3-class open-vocabulary systems
it is <em id="S5.SS3.p2.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">goal verification at the stopping decision</em>, making the
<math id="S5.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80.2\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>80.2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80.2\,\%</annotation></semantics></math> false-stop share the primary open
problem (§<a href="#S6" title="6 Discussion ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Discussion</h2>

<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpreting SPL across simulation regimes.</h5>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GOAT-Bench</span> literature has forked into two operating
regimes. The <em id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">strict physical regime</em>
(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a></cite>; Modular GOAT, SenseAct-NN,
TANGO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, AnyGoal) fixes discrete
<math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25\,\mathrm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25\,\mathrm{m}</annotation></semantics></math> steps, <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> turns, a <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="42^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>42</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">42^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> HFOV
(HelloRobot Stretch), and <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">allow_sliding=False</span>. A
<em id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">relaxed continuous regime</em> used by
3D-Mem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> and DORAEMON <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>
substitutes Habitat’s oracle pathfinder (collapsing the SPL
trajectory denominator from thousands of steps to a handful of
waypoints) and a <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="120^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>120</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">120^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> HFOV camera; we read 3D-Mem’s
<math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="44.7\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>44.7</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">44.7\,\%</annotation></semantics></math> SPL as a measurement under a different evaluation
contract rather than a comparable upper bound on AnyGoal’s
<math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12.7\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12.7</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12.7\,\%</annotation></semantics></math>. Inside the strict regime, AnyGoal’s SPL exceeds
SenseAct-NN (<math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12.7</annotation></semantics></math> vs <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11.3</annotation></semantics></math>); the marginal deficits to Modular GOAT
and TANGO (<math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\!-\!4.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\!-\!4.5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\!-\!3.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\!-\!3.8</annotation></semantics></math> pp) are the direct cost of the
<math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+27.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>27.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+27.5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+20.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>20.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+20.3</annotation></semantics></math> pp Subtask SR advantages under a uniform BVM
prior that physically tests more frontiers per subtask.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Limitations and Future Work</h2>

<section id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Transparent-object floor (perception assumption).</h5>

<div id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Twelve goal categories (<em id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">glass</em>, <em id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">shower glass</em>,
<em id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">handrail</em>, <math id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>) score <math id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\,\%</annotation></semantics></math> SR across all four detector
backbones because the GoalProjector cannot anchor a back-projection on
transparent, thin, or specular surfaces; a DistGate
<span id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">proj_dist=None</span> edge case further accepts <span id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</span> when
no depth is available (one-line patch and a monocular-depth fusion
remedy in Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E The Transparent-Object Floor and DistGate ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Odometry and centralized-simulator assumption.</h5>

<div id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">BVM fusion assumes consistent BEV alignment across agents; the
real-world deployment relies on Vicon ground truth to isolate this
variable, and GPS-denied operation at scale would require onboard
SLAM or UWB-anchored relative localization. The simulator further
shares the BVM as an in-process tensor; multi-machine deployment
would require explicit map synchronization with non-trivial bandwidth
(<math id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim\!18\,\mathrm{MB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>MB</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim\!18\,\mathrm{MB}</annotation></semantics></math> per full BEV broadcast).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Single-run evaluation.</h5>

<div id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Due to the compute constraints noted in §4, each ablation cell is a single rollout. A second-seed re-run of the headline configuration is provided (Appendix <a href="#A4.SS5" title="D.5 Headline-run reproducibility ‣ Appendix D Extended Results ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a>), but a multi-seeded sweep across all backbones remains future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Path efficiency gap (future work).</h5>

<div id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">AnyGoal’s strict-regime SPL (<math id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12.7\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12.7</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12.7\,\%</annotation></semantics></math>) trails Modular GOAT
(<math id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="17.2\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>17.2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">17.2\,\%</annotation></semantics></math>) and TANGO (<math id="S7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16.5\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16.5</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16.5\,\%</annotation></semantics></math>) by 3–5 pp because a uniform BVM
prior obliges the agent to physically test more frontiers per subtask.
Two avenues preserve zero-shot generalization while closing this gap:
pre-priming the BVM from a VLM layout caption (“ovens lie near
sinks”), or distilling AnyGoal trajectories into a learned policy
over BVM features while keeping the discrete physical action space.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AnyGoal</span> is a decentralized, training-free multi-agent
architecture that fuses VLM common sense with a lightweight 2D
Gaussian Bayesian Value Map. On <span id="S8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GOAT-Bench</span> <em id="S8.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">val_unseen</em>
it reaches <span id="S8.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">52.4 %</span> Subtask SR (<span id="S8.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">+27.5 pp</span> over
Modular GOAT) at <math id="S8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!2</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="S8.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">41.9 %</span> at <math id="S8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!1</annotation></semantics></math>, a new
state-of-the-art in the strict physical regime; the gain is
architectural rather than a function of agent count, and under SAM3
<math id="S8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80.2\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>80.2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80.2\,\%</annotation></semantics></math> of failures are <em id="S8.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">false stops</em>, shifting the open
problem of zero-shot navigation from <em id="S8.p1.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">finding</em> the goal to
<em id="S8.p1.1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">verifying</em> it at the stopping decision.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="S8.SS0.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Acknowledgments</h4>

<div id="S8.SS0.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The authors thank the Intelligent Space Robotics
Laboratory at Skoltech for compute access and the open-source maintainers
of Habitat-Sim, SAM3, GroundingDINO, YOLO-World, CLIP, and DINOv2 for
their continued contributions to embodied-AI research. <em id="S8.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Code,
configurations, and trajectory logs will be released at the
camera-ready stage.</em></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
