</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Map representation and in-process fusion</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">AnyGoal runs as a single Python process; the <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> agents share GPU
memory and there is no inter-process map synchronization in the
simulator. Each agent maintains an individual semantic map tensor
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{full\_map}[j]\in\mathbb{R}^{20\times 480\times 480}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">full_map</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>480</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>480</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{full\_map}[j]\in\mathbb{R}^{20\times 480\times 480}</annotation></semantics></math> with
the following channel allocation:</p>
<table id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Channel</span></th>
<th id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Content</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.SS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.SS2.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">0</th>
<td id="A1.SS2.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Obstacle occupancy</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.SS2.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">1</th>
<td id="A1.SS2.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Explored mask</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.SS2.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">2</th>
<td id="A1.SS2.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Current agent position</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS2.p1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.SS2.p1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">3</th>
<td id="A1.SS2.p1.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Visited mask</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.SS2.p1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.SS2.p1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">4–19</th>
<td id="A1.SS2.p1.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Semantic category one-hots</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Every global step the agent maps are merged by element-wise max,
<code id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">full_map_pred, _ = torch.max(full_map2, 0)</code> (<span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">main.py:2285</span>),
yielding a conservative union BEV used immediately for frontier
extraction (<span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Frontiers()</span>, <span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">main.py:2286</span>) and BVM
scoring.
A single <span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BayesianValueMap</span> object is instantiated once and
shared across all agents (not per-agent); any agent that detects the
goal at confidence <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\!0.30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\!0.30</annotation></semantics></math> triggers
<span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">update_value_map()</span> (<span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">vlm_agents.py:561--585</span>), which
writes directly into the shared map. The real-world deployment
(§<a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Real-World Heterogeneous Deployment ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>) replaces this with a ROS2 occupancy-grid
broadcast at 2 Hz.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>VLM Prompt Templates</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All prompts are in <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">src/SystemPrompt.py</span>. Placeholders are shown
in braces; the GOAT-context header (subtask index, current goal,
modality, remaining budget) is prepended verbatim to every prompt at
<span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SystemPrompt.py:563--591</span>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Scene caption (<span id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Stage1-Caption</span>)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<blockquote id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">You are guiding a robot to find a target object indoors. Describe the
scene BRIEFLY:</span></p>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(1) Room type (kitchen / bedroom / living room / bathroom / hallway /
stairwell / other).
(2) Key objects seen (name, direction, approximate distance in meters).
(3) Openings (doors, corridors, stairs) and which directions are
unexplored.
(4) Target hint: is the target visible? If not, does the room type or
visible objects suggest it could be nearby?</span></p>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Be concise — 3–5 sentences maximum.</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Is-worth gate (<span id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Stage3-Gate</span>)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">System prompt (<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SystemPrompt.py:426--437</span>):</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<blockquote id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">You are deciding whether the robot should keep exploring THIS direction
to find a target object.</span></p>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If the detector found the target with confidence <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{&gt;}80\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{&gt;}80\%</annotation></semantics></math>: answer
<span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Yes</span>.
If the room type matches the target’s typical location (e.g. stove
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> kitchen, bed <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> bedroom, staircase handrail
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> hallway/stairwell): answer <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Yes</span>.
If co-located objects are visible (e.g. microwave near stove,
nightstand near bed): answer <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Yes</span>.
If the room clearly cannot contain the target (e.g. looking for a
staircase handrail in a bedroom): answer <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No</span>.
Ignore generic objects (doors, walls, light switches).</span></p>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Output ONLY: Yes or No. Nothing else.</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">User template (<span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SystemPrompt.py:622--630</span>):</p>
<blockquote id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">- Target of navigation: {TARGET}
<br class="ltx_break">- Common-sense placement: A "{TARGET}" is typically found
{PLACEMENT_HINT}.
<br class="ltx_break">- Scene object (Object Detection): {OBJECT_DETECTION}
<br class="ltx_break">Decision:
</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The Yes/No response is parsed into a probability
<math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Perception\_PR}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Perception</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>PR</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Perception\_PR}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> via first-token logit extraction
(max_new_tokens<math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,=\," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,=\,</annotation></semantics></math>8). The downstream gate at
<span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SystemPrompt.py:682</span> applies threshold <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.50</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Frontier vs. history (<span id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Stage-FN</span>)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">System prompt (<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SystemPrompt.py:441--467</span>), summarized:
the VLM is shown a top-down semantic map with frontier candidates
(black dots, uppercase letters A–D), historical observation points
(green dots, lowercase letters a–d), and the robot’s pose, and asked
to answer Yes (explore a new frontier) or No (revisit a historical
point). Decision rules emphasize distance efficiency for SPL, room-type
priors, exploration–exploitation balance, collision-trap detection,
and directional continuity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Frontier ABCD selection (<span id="A2.SS4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Stage4-Select</span>)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">System prompt (<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SystemPrompt.py:470--517</span>). The VLM is given
the same top-down semantic map plus the robot’s egocentric view; for
each labeled frontier it estimates (i) distance, (ii) target
probability under a common-sense placement prior, (iii) an efficiency
score <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math> target probability <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="/" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>/</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">/</annotation></semantics></math> distance. The output is constrained
to a single letter <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\in\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in\{</annotation></semantics></math>A, B, C, D<math id="A2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which the parser converts to
the softmax over markers. The historical-point variant
(<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SystemPrompt.py:523--551</span>) follows the same template with
lowercase markers.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Per-Agent Decision Loop</h2>

<figure id="A3.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A3.fig1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">
<span id="A3.fig1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:331.2pt;">
<span id="A3.fig1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.fig1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1: AnyGoal – one decision step per agent <math id="A3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:2.0pt;"></span>
<span id="A3.fig1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inputs:</span> RGB-D observation <math id="A3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>, current goal token
<math id="A3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, shared BEV <math id="A3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, shared BVM <math id="A3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}=(\mu,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}=(\mu,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>,
previous frontier <math id="A3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{prev}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext>prev</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{prev}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>, peers’ selections
<math id="A3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f_{j}^{\star}\}_{j&lt;i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f_{j}^{\star}\}_{j&lt;i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
<span id="A3.fig1.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.fig1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hyperparameters:</span> <math id="A3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (UCB), <math id="A3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> (blend), <math id="A3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>sep</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math>
(separation radius), <math id="A3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> (separation factor), <math id="A3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=1.5</annotation></semantics></math> (hysteresis),
<math id="A3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=25</annotation></semantics></math> (re-eval interval), <math id="A3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{worth}}=0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>worth</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{worth}}=0.50</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
<span id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.6em;">
<span id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Perception.</span> Run open-vocabulary detector on
<math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> for goal <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; back-project hits through depth-cone mask
into the shared BEV.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">BVM update.</span> For each visible cell <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{\text{obs}},\sigma^{2}_{\text{obs}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>obs</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>obs</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{\text{obs}},\sigma^{2}_{\text{obs}})</annotation></semantics></math>, apply
Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.2 Gaussian Bayesian Value Map ‣ 3 Method ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Merge.</span> <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\leftarrow\max_{j}\texttt{full\_map}[j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">full_map</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\leftarrow\max_{j}\texttt{full\_map}[j]</annotation></semantics></math>
(element-wise across agents).</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Frontiers.</span> Extract <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from
connected-component boundary of <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\bmod\Delta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\bmod\Delta=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> run the VLM prompt chain
(scene caption <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> is-worth gate <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> frontier softmax) to obtain
<math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{VLM}}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{VLM}}(f)</annotation></semantics></math> and the gate score
<math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Perception\_PR}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Perception</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>PR</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Perception\_PR}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Perception\_PR}&lt;\tau_{\text{worth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Perception</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>PR</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>worth</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Perception\_PR}&lt;\tau_{\text{worth}}</annotation></semantics></math>, set
<math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{VLM}}(\cdot)\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{VLM}}(\cdot)\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Score.</span> For each <math id="A3.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A3.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(f)\leftarrow\mu(f)+\beta\sqrt{\sigma^{2}(f)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(f)\leftarrow\mu(f)+\beta\sqrt{\sigma^{2}(f)}</annotation></semantics></math>;
<math id="A3.I1.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(f)\leftarrow(1-w)\,p_{\text{VLM}}(f)+w\,\widetilde{U}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(f)\leftarrow(1-w)\,p_{\text{VLM}}(f)+w\,\widetilde{U}(f)</annotation></semantics></math>,
with <math id="A3.I1.i6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{U}</annotation></semantics></math> min-max normalized over <math id="A3.I1.i6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">7.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Allocate.</span> <math id="A3.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}^{\star}\leftarrow\arg\max_{f}s(f)\cdot\prod_{j&lt;i}\phi(d(f,f_{j}^{\star}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}^{\star}\leftarrow\arg\max_{f}s(f)\cdot\prod_{j&lt;i}\phi(d(f,f_{j}^{\star}))</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A3.I1.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(d){=}0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(d){=}0.6</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A3.I1.i7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d{&lt;}D_{\text{sep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>sep</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d{&lt;}D_{\text{sep}}</annotation></semantics></math> else <math id="A3.I1.i7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">8.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hysteresis.</span> Switch from <math id="A3.I1.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{prev}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext>prev</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{prev}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="A3.I1.i8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> only if
<math id="A3.I1.i8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(f_{i}^{\star})\geq\eta\,s(f_{\text{prev}}^{(i)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext>prev</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(f_{i}^{\star})\geq\eta\,s(f_{\text{prev}}^{(i)})</annotation></semantics></math>;
otherwise hold <math id="A3.I1.i8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{prev}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext>prev</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{prev}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">9.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Plan and act.</span> FMM plan from current pose to
<math id="A3.I1.i9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>; execute one discrete action in
<math id="A3.I1.i9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textsc{forward},\textsc{left},\textsc{right},\textsc{stop}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">forward</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">left</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">right</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textsc{forward},\textsc{left},\textsc{right},\textsc{stop}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">10.</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I1.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DistGate STOP check.</span> If <span id="A3.I1.i10.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</span> is selected,
reject it if the goal projection distance exceeds <math id="A3.I1.i10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.0\,\mathrm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.0\,\mathrm{m}</annotation></semantics></math>
(§<a href="#A5" title="Appendix E The Transparent-Object Floor and DistGate ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>); otherwise emit <span id="A3.I1.i10.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</span>.</span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></p>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Source pointers for each step: BVM update in
<span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">mapping/bayesian_value_map.py:219</span>;
score blend in <span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">main.py:2735--2738</span>; separation penalty in
<span id="A3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">main.py:2746--2759</span>; hysteresis in <span id="A3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">main.py:2804--2832</span>;
DistGate in <span id="A3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">main.py:3239--3253</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Extended Results</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
