<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The bi-modal failure cohort (false stops cluster near 41 steps; budget
exhaustions sit at the 500-step ceiling) substantiates the body claim
that, under a high-recall detector, the dominant failure mode is
premature <span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</span> rather than incomplete exploration.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Two-proportion <math id="A4.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>-tests for Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 5.3 Perception bottleneck ablation (the 4-way test) ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Computed from the verified <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n_{\text{total}},n_{\text{succ}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>succ</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n_{\text{total}},n_{\text{succ}})</annotation></semantics></math> counts
above using the pooled-variance two-proportion <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>-test
(<math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(\hat{p}_{1}-\hat{p}_{2})/\sqrt{\hat{p}(1-\hat{p})(1/n_{1}+1/n_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(\hat{p}_{1}-\hat{p}_{2})/\sqrt{\hat{p}(1-\hat{p})(1/n_{1}+1/n_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math>;
<math id="A4.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}</annotation></semantics></math> pooled).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T12" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span><span id="A4.T12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Two-proportion <math id="A4.T12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>-tests on detector-ablation Subtask
SR differences.</span> The recall-tier transition (rows 2, 4, 5) is
significant at <math id="A4.T12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\!&lt;\!10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">&lt;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\!&lt;\!10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>; within-tier gaps (rows 1, 3) are not
significant at <math id="A4.T12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.05</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
