 ns <math id="A4.T12.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\!\geq\!0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\!\geq\!0.05</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A4.T12.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is the subtask-level success fraction
(<math id="A4.T12.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{succ}}/n_{\text{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>succ</mtext></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{succ}}/n_{\text{total}}</annotation></semantics></math>); the small gap to the
episode-averaged <span id="A4.T12.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">goat_SR</span> in Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 5.3 Perception bottleneck ablation (the 4-way test) ‣ 5 Results and Evaluation ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>
(<math id="A4.T12.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq\!0.005" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.005</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq\!0.005</annotation></semantics></math>) does not affect any significance conclusion.</p></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Headline-run reproducibility</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The headline <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!2</annotation></semantics></math> SAM3+CLIP configuration was re-run on a second
simulator seed over the full <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="360" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>360</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">360</annotation></semantics></math>-episode split. The two seeds are
effectively identical (Table <a href="#A4.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ D.5 Headline-run reproducibility ‣ Appendix D Extended Results ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>): Subtask SR differs by
<math id="A4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.29" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.29</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.29</annotation></semantics></math> pp and SPL by <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math> pp. We therefore report the headline result
as <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="52.4\,\%\pm 0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>52.4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">52.4\,\%\pm 0.2</annotation></semantics></math> pp Subtask SR over two seeds, and use seed 1
throughout the main paper.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T13" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span><span id="A4.T13.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Two-seed reproducibility</span> of the headline <math id="A4.T13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!2</annotation></semantics></math>
SAM3+CLIP configuration on the full <span id="A4.T13.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GOAT-Bench</span>
<em id="A4.T13.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">val_unseen</em> split.</figcaption>
