<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>The Transparent-Object Floor and DistGate</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Twelve goal categories score <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\,\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\,\%</annotation></semantics></math> subtask SR across all four
detector backbones: <em id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">glass</em> (0/44), <em id="A5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">shower glass</em> (0/13),
<em id="A5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">book</em> (0/45), <em id="A5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">boiler</em> (0/12), <em id="A5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">christmas tree</em> (0/18),
<em id="A5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">footrest</em> (0/10), <em id="A5.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hanging clothes</em> (0/46), <em id="A5.p1.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">photo</em>
(0/9), and four other context-dependent categories
(<em id="A5.p1.1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">parapet</em>, <em id="A5.p1.1.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">handrail</em>, <em id="A5.p1.1.11" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">stair</em>, <em id="A5.p1.1.12" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exercise bike</em>).
Two failure paths converge on these categories.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Depth unreliability.</span> Transparent (<em id="A5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">glass</em>,
<em id="A5.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">shower glass</em>), reflective, and thin-flat (<em id="A5.p2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">photo</em>,
<em id="A5.p2.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">calendar</em>) goals are detected in RGB by the VLM but the depth
channel is absent or noisy, so the GoalProjector cannot back-project
the detection to a stable BEV cell. Without a depth anchor the BVM
is never updated for these categories, leaving them invisible to the
frontier planner.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DistGate edge case.</span> The current STOP gate
(<span id="A5.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">main.py:3239--3253</span>) rejects <span id="A5.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</span> when the goal
projection distance exceeds <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{max\_stop\_dist}=3.0\,\mathrm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">max_stop_dist</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{max\_stop\_dist}=3.0\,\mathrm{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,
but logs and <em id="A5.p3.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">accepts</em> <span id="A5.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">stop</span> when no projection is
available at all:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<blockquote id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">elif pdist is None:
<br class="ltx_break"> logging.info(f"[DistGate] Agent_{ai}: STOP requested but "
<br class="ltx_break">      f"no proj_dist available (GoalProjector didn’t detect).")
<br class="ltx_break"> # action[ai] remains 0 (STOP) --- NOT overridden
</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">A one-line patch (<code id="A5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">action[ai] = 1</code>) converts the no-projection
branch from a logging hole into a hard STOP rejection, requiring depth
evidence at every stop:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<blockquote id="A5.p6.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">elif pdist is None:
<br class="ltx_break"> logging.info(f"[DistGate] Agent_{ai}: STOP requested but "
<br class="ltx_break">      f"no proj_dist available --- STOP rejected.")
<br class="ltx_break"> action[ai] = 1 # override: no depth, no stop
</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div id="A5.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Categories expected to recover under the patch are those that fail
through under-projected detections rather than truly invisible RGB
signals (e.g. <em id="A5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">photo</em>, where the GroundedSAM run logs <math id="A5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math> false
stops at <math id="A5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.3\,\mathrm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4.3</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.3\,\mathrm{m}</annotation></semantics></math> average euclidean distance to goal). Glass
and shower-glass categories, which fail through absent RGB detections,
remain inaccessible to this patch and motivate the monocular-depth
fusion line of future work in §<a href="#S7" title="7 Limitations and Future Work ‣ AnyGoal: Vision-Language Guided Multi-Agent Exploration for Training-Free Lifelong Navigation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Compute Profile</h2>

<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Wall clock.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The headline run
(<span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">goat_full_val_unseen_20260408.log</span>, 2-agent SAM3+CLIP,
seed 1, 360 episodes, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="320{,}247" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>320,247</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">320{,}247</annotation></semantics></math> global timesteps) terminated at
<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6\,\text{d}\,01\,\text{h}\,50\,\text{m}\,53\,\text{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 01</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>h</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 50</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>m</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 53</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>s</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\,\text{d}\,01\,\text{h}\,50\,\text{m}\,53\,\text{s}</annotation></semantics></math>
<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx\!145.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>145.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx\!145.8</annotation></semantics></math> wall-clock hours on a single NVIDIA RTX 4090
(<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\!16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\!16</annotation></semantics></math> GB VRAM peak).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Per-stage VLM latency.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[VLM-LAT]</span> instrumentation tag was added after the headline
run, so per-stage latency below is measured on the seed 2 re-run
(<span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">goat_sam3_clip_2agent_seed2_20260521_205309.log</span>, same
configuration, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="249" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>249</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">249</annotation></semantics></math> episodes at audit time). The model identifier,
hardware, decoding parameters, and code path are identical; the
numbers therefore represent the headline system but are not the
headline run itself.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T14" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 14: </span><span id="A6.T14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Per-stage VLM latency</span> (mean / median / P10 / P90, in
